@startuml
skinparam {
    ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    BoundaryBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ControlBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    EntityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

actor User
boundary "Story Detail Page (UI)" as UI
boundary Router
control ChapterController
control ChapterService
entity HistoryModel
entity ChapterModel
database MongoDB

User -> UI: 1. Open story detail
activate User
activate UI

UI -> Router: 2. GET /history/{userId}/{storyId}
activate Router

Router -> ChapterController: 3. getLastReadChapterFromHistory()
activate ChapterController

ChapterController -> ChapterController: 4. Parse params & convert ObjectId
activate ChapterController
ChapterController -> ChapterService: 5. getLastReadChapterFromHistory(user_id, story_id)
deactivate ChapterController

activate ChapterService
ChapterService -> HistoryModel: 6. Find history by user & story
activate HistoryModel

HistoryModel -> MongoDB: 7. findOne({user_id, story_id})
activate MongoDB
MongoDB --> HistoryModel: 8. History document
deactivate MongoDB

HistoryModel -> ChapterModel: 9. Populate last_read_chapter
activate ChapterModel
ChapterModel -> MongoDB: 10. Find chapter by ID
activate MongoDB
MongoDB --> ChapterModel: 11. Chapter document
deactivate MongoDB
ChapterModel --> HistoryModel: 12. Chapter data
deactivate ChapterModel

HistoryModel --> ChapterService: 13. History with last_read_chapter
deactivate HistoryModel

ChapterService --> ChapterController: 14. Return history result
deactivate ChapterService
ChapterController --> Router: 15. HTTP response
deactivate ChapterController

Router --> UI: 16. Show last read chapter
deactivate Router
UI --> User: 17. Display continue reading
deactivate UI
deactivate User
@enduml
